    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties, plainly. This was trip TRP-02828, booked as a 9.0 km / 13.0 min route (EV-TRIP-02828) but driven at 14.4 km. The rider was charged $20.66 (charged_total on the fare breakdown EV-FARE-02828).\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02828) measures the trip at 14.4 km, an excess of 5.4 km — 60.0% of the optimal route, both POL-RD-01 tests passed and, being over 50%, a MATERIAL deviation. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern over the rounded copy on the trip record, and the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07: 114 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps over 90 seconds, no straight-line jump over 500 m. The deviation therefore stands on the trace alone and the rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged.\n\nTHE 'ROAD WORKS' EXPLANATION CARRIES NO WEIGHT. No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-02828-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and no payload, and the driver named no advisory ID. Under POL-RD-13 the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run on this record, so the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, no closure-adjusted optimal exists, and the excess stands at the measured 5.4 km. Because the driver cited no artifact for an advisory, POL-RD-13(1) applies and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged — this is a gap in the bundle, not an escalation.\n\nTHE REFUND, under POL-RD-02, on this METERED fare (fare_model METERED; quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not displace POL-RD-02): recomputed_fare = (base 3.80 + 0.75 x 9.0 km + 0.28 x 13.0 min) x surge_multiplier 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-02828, + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls + 0 waiting fee - 0 promo = $14.99. Refund = charged_total $20.66 - $14.99 = $5.67, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = $5.70. That is above the $0.50 de minimis and 27.4% of the charge — below the 90% full-refund share — so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of $5.70, and the driver retains the remaining $14.96 of the fare.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. On the driver's argument that the refund cannot exceed the $4.00 shown as amount_contested_sgd: I reject it. POL-RD-02 fixes the refund as charged_total less recomputed_fare, and its FULL_REFUND test is itself stated against charged_total ('90% or more of charged_total'). No clause caps a refund at the figure named when filing; the policy's ceilings are SGD 150.00 and charged_total, neither approached here. On the POL-RD-06 check that the material deviation forces: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 2 (below 3) and 2 / 180 completed_trips_90d is 0.011 (below 0.05), so no repeat-deviation pattern is established — no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01 and is not used. On POL-RD-09: there are zero ERP/toll lines and no airport surcharge (this trip neither originates nor ends at an airport), so no pass-through correction adds to or subtracts from the POL-RD-02 figure, and no billing-integrity referral arises. On the driver-side clauses: the chat log is empty (no POL-RD-04 instruction), no pickup or dropoff amendment exists (POL-RD-05 unavailable), and vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12 inapplicable), so the 9.0 km booked optimal is the correct comparator. No driver compensation arises: the distance billed (14.4 km) equals the distance driven, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-kilometre limb has nothing to compute.\n\nEFFECT. The monetary effect is $5.70, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it is executed automatically on issue; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
